“ISLAMIC NATO” FACES ITS FIRST REAL TEST — AND THE WORLD IS WATCHING!
 Saudi Arabia was hit by a major Houthi missile-and-drone assault, leaving 73 people injured and hitting critical energy facilities.
Then came the big question:
Where is Pakistan?
The Makkah Defence Pact says an attack on one member is an attack on all.
Yet Pakistan’s initial response was condemnation and diplomatic support—not troops.
 A pact that promised “one for all” is now facing its first battlefield test.
Pakistan’s Defence Minister has warned that the pact could become operational if the conflict spills further into Saudi territory.
Will Pakistan fight—or will the “Islamic NATO” remain only a promise on paper?

